// The core format: the structured document syntax every Heron file is written in.
include = [
  "./files.heron",
  "./nodes.heron",
  "./naming.heron",
  "./imports.heron",
  "./mounts.heron.md",
  "./exports.heron.md",
  "./amends.heron",
  "./conflicts.heron",
  "./values.heron",
  "./expressions.heron.md",
  "./prose_layer.heron",
  "./code_layer.heron.md",
  "./tour.heron.md",
]

@lens(user, developer)
| The structured document syntax every [Heron file](#language.core_format.files.heron_file) is written in. It defines no kinds of its own: **Heron**, the specification language, builds on it with packages for types, APIs, rules, scenarios and prompts. Its files end in `.heron` and its tool is the `heron` binary.
